<title>UK: Low &amp; Bonar chairman Laughland to retire.</title>
<headline>Low &amp; Bonar chairman Laughland to retire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Low &amp; Bonar Plc said its chairman of the last three years, Hugh Laughland, is to retire later this year.</p>
<p>Laughland, who is 65, has agreed to stay on as chairman until late summer when John Robinson will take over the position, the company said in its annual report.</p>
<p>Robinson was appointed a non-executive director on August 6 last year and is currently deputy chairman and chief executive of Smith &amp; Nephew Plc.</p>
<p>A resolution proposing that Laughland continue as a director will be put to the forthcoming annual meeting.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
